        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order confirmed; event-level review remains incomplete\n\nThe relevant order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Required item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Not available in the accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not available |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event type, timing, and recorded status |\n\nThe accessible records contain the work order, cost period, and Oracle policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. The supporting event records are restricted to the records-custodian role. I requested an authorized extract, but none was received. This is **not evidence that no late event exists**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are **not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before the cutoff continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary new transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held from processing while the period remains Pending Close. I cannot conclude whether the actual recorded status follows that rule without the authorized event evidence.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_d567a7cc50c5/audit-report.json`; the submitted report is marked **needs_evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
